# /etc/aicc-edge/edge.env for the STAGING host (mode 0640, owner root:aicc-edge). Rendered by `install-stack.sh --only edge-env --acme-email <addr>`: the stage id is read from
# /etc/aicc-stage-identity (AICC_STAGE_ID, generated by the `identity` step) so the identity route of the Caddyfile, the site build and deploy-release.sh all use ONE value.
# The installer never overwrites an existing file. KEY=VALUE, values with spaces in double quotes. NO secrets belong here.
# Variable names and semantics are those of docs/cutover/Caddyfile.edge.template and scripts/ops/edge-preflight.sh (the edge/cutover work owns them); this file only fills them in for
# the Linux layout of infra/provision: static site and CP releases under /srv/aicc/<kind>/current, PHP-FPM pool socket /run/php/aicc-cp.sock.
# DEVIATION to confirm with the Caddyfile owner: scripts/ops/render-edge.mjs --env-template suggests AICC_WP_ROOT=/srv/aicc/cp/current/wp; the Control Plane release tree here has
# WordPress at its ROOT (wp-config.php and uploads are symlinks into /srv/aicc/shared), so the docroot is /srv/aicc/cp/current. Same variable, different value, no template change.
AICC_EDGE_MODE=stage
AICC_PUBLIC_HOST=stage.copilt.org
AICC_STAGE_HOST=stage.copilt.org
AICC_STAGE_ID=__STAGE_ID__
AICC_STATIC_ROOT=/srv/aicc/site/current
AICC_WP_ROOT=/srv/aicc/cp/current
AICC_PHP_FPM_SOCKET=unix//run/php/aicc-cp.sock
AICC_ACME_EMAIL=__ACME_EMAIL__
# FIRST start only: the Let's Encrypt STAGING directory (rate limits; browsers do not trust its certificates). After section 6 of docs/cutover/stage-linux.md passes, DELETE this line
# and `systemctl reload aicc-edge` so Caddy requests the real certificate (RUNBOOK-stage-bringup.md step 8).
AICC_ACME_CA=https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
AICC_LOG_DIR=/var/log/aicc-edge
AICC_ADMIN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:12019
AICC_OPERATOR_PORT=8443
AICC_WP_TIMEOUT=60s
# AICC_OPERATOR_CIDRS stays unset: stage and production have NO public operator allowlist (the preflight refuses a non-empty value); operators use the SSH tunnel to the loopback listener.
# HTTP/3 stays OFF: udp/443 is closed in UFW and in the cloud firewall; the Caddyfile sets `protocols h1 h2` and no Alt-Svc.
